From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: do not advertise hot-plug on the q706f root port

The only device behind the SM8250 PCIe0 root port is the soldered QCA6390.
The root port advertises Hot-Plug Capable; with CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE unset,
pciehp_is_native() is false, so pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 for the
port (before pcie_port_pm=force is even looked at). In s2idle
dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() then sees pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() == false,
keeps the link in L0/L1 and the controller clocks (aux, refgen <- GPLL0/CXO)
stay on, holding a CXO vote: no SoC deep sleep (cxsd/aosd/ddr stay 0).

Status: under test (14.11.2026). Not applied to the series yet.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -397,6 +397,15 @@
 	 * Attention Button Present in Slot Capabilities.
 	 */
 	val &= ~PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_ABP;
+
+	/*
+	 * q706f: the only device (QCA6390 Wi-Fi) is soldered down. A Root Port
+	 * that advertises Hot-Plug Capable while pciehp is not built is never
+	 * allowed into D3 (pci_bridge_d3_possible()), so the host never sends
+	 * PME_Turn_Off / enters L2 in suspend and the controller clocks keep
+	 * a CXO vote. Do not advertise hot-plug.
+	 */
+	val &= ~(PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC | PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPS);
 	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 
 	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
